## Circuit-Sword WiFi preseed -- NOT a drop-in file, see below.
##
## CORRECTED after real hardware testing (2026-08-04): dropping a
## batocera.conf file onto the boot partition, or hand-editing
## /userdata/system/batocera.conf directly over SSH, does NOT reliably
## get picked up -- batocera.conf is not live-watched, and a raw file
## edit was confirmed on-device to not take effect even after reboot.
## The values below only take effect through the tool that actually
## triggers config application:
##
## FURTHER CONFIRMED (2026-08-05): hand-editing /boot/batocera-boot.conf
## directly on the SD card (e.g. via a Mac-mounted /Volumes/BATOCERA/
## batocera-boot.conf) is an explicit trap, not just "doesn't get
## picked up" -- it DOES work, but only for the device's very first
## boot ever (S08connman falls back to reading boot.conf only while
## /userdata/system/batocera.conf doesn't exist yet, and never copies
## those values into /userdata). The first shutdown after that then
## runs S65values4boot, which syncs boot.conf FROM the (still-blank)
## /userdata master -- silently erasing whatever you hand-edited into
## boot.conf. Net effect: WiFi works for exactly one boot, then reverts
## to disabled on every boot after, looking like it "turned itself off".
## Editing boot.conf is a one-shot bootstrap at best -- always also (or
## instead) do Option A or B below on the live system.
##
## Option A -- EmulationStation UI (confirmed working on real hardware):
##   Menu (Start) -> Network Settings -> enable WiFi, fill in SSID/password.
##
## Option B -- SSH, using the settings CLI (not a raw file edit):
##   ssh root@<device-ip>
##   batocera-settings-set wifi.enabled 1
##   batocera-settings-set wifi.ssid "YOUR_SSID"
##   batocera-settings-set wifi.key "YOUR_WIFI_PASSWORD"
##   reboot
##
## Either path writes into /userdata/system/batocera.conf for you and
## applies it correctly. NEVER paste your real SSID/password into chat
## or commit them anywhere -- enter them directly on the device.
##
## Reference: the raw keys these tools set (for context only -- do not
## place this content as a standalone file and expect it to be read):
## package/batocera/core/batocera-system/batocera.conf (lines ~104-113)

wifi.enabled=1
wifi.country=NL
wifi.ssid=YOUR_SSID_HERE
wifi.key=YOUR_WIFI_PASSWORD_HERE
system.hostname=CIRCUITSWORD
